{"base_rate":0.266754270696452,"brier":0.13780078843626806,"bss":0.29548413228101766,"bss_hi":0.42429347492330843,"bss_lo":0.12992857402337826,"chart":{"base":[292.6,164.6],"fp":[197.8,121.4],"lead":"62,257.9 272,237.7 482,212.7 692,164.8","note":{"base":"skill 0.30 — higher than 54% of cities","fp":"low end -1pp, high end +29pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.0 °C — better than 61% of cities","rel":"promised 1% → rained 2%; promised 92% → rained 63%"},"rel":"69.3,458.8 263.9,452.3 639.9,192.6"},"country":"JP","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.17605781865965833,"ess":479.38908189300963,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Osaka</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Osaka rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (98%), believe about\n<b>78%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>0%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 761 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 2.1 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.30, ranked 99 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(47&ndash;169) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>0%</b></td><td class='num'>216</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'><b>5%</b></td><td class='num'>82</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>19%</td><td class='num'><b>1%</b></td><td class='num'>81</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>45%</td><td class='num'><b>5%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>73%</td><td class='num'><b>18%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>98%</td><td class='num'><b>78%</b></td><td class='num'>229</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Osaka</b> <span class=\"muted\">Japan</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;27% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 27% of days.</p><p>The forecast did better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">5 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.30</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>47&ndash;169\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>761 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Osaka &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Osaka\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.01638888888889,382.0 72.85073170731707,350.8158536585372 126.48370370370371,278.641975308642 218.77116883116886,174.0 318.00368421052633,80.26315789473682 404.2243668122271,19.589519650655006 404.2243668122271,32.30567685589517 318.00368421052633,152.10526315789474 218.77116883116886,254.36363636363637 126.48370370370371,341.55555555555554 72.85073170731707,382.0 58.01638888888889,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"284.90144546649145\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"284.90144546649145\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.01638888888889,380.31481481481484 72.85073170731707,364.2439024390244 126.48370370370371,377.5061728395062 218.77116883116886,363.09090909090907 318.00368421052633,314.9473684210526 404.2243668122271,97.47598253275106\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 0% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 216 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.01638888888889\" cy=\"380.31481481481484\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 4%&amp;#10;It rained 5% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 82 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"72.85073170731707\" cy=\"364.2439024390244\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 19%&amp;#10;It rained 1% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 81 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"126.48370370370371\" cy=\"377.5061728395062\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 45%&amp;#10;It rained 5% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"218.77116883116886\" cy=\"363.09090909090907\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 73%&amp;#10;It rained 18% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"318.00368421052633\" cy=\"314.9473684210526\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 98%&amp;#10;It rained 78% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 229 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"404.2243668122271\" cy=\"97.47598253275106\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(27%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Osaka the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.57) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (-0.01).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>14%</td><td class='num'>-0.005</td><td class='num'>15.1%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>29%</td><td class='num'>0.065</td><td class='num'>25.8%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>182</td><td class='num'>28%</td><td class='num'>0.254</td><td class='num'>17.7%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>220</td><td class='num'>34%</td><td class='num'>0.572</td><td class='num'>12.8%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":34.69379,"lon":135.50107,"n":761,"n_cities":216,"name":"Osaka","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.02,"lo":0.0,"mean":4.6296296296296294e-05,"n":216,"obs":0.004629629629629629,"sig":true},{"hi":0.1,"lo":0.02,"mean":0.041951219512195125,"n":82,"obs":0.04878048780487805,"sig":false},{"hi":0.33,"lo":0.1,"mean":0.1934567901234568,"n":81,"obs":0.012345679012345678,"sig":true},{"hi":0.61,"lo":0.33,"mean":0.45415584415584426,"n":77,"obs":0.05194805194805195,"sig":true},{"hi":0.84,"lo":0.61,"mean":0.7344736842105263,"n":76,"obs":0.18421052631578946,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.84,"mean":0.9780349344978166,"n":229,"obs":0.7816593886462883,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":2.1,"provisional":false,"rank":99,"rank_hi":169.0,"rank_lo":46.95,"reliability":0.06171438998031584,"resolution":0.11664224763781944,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"osaka","station":"","timezone":"Asia/Tokyo"}